<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Code-to-model traceability: 91/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Modelling functions in 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py consistently cite specific sections, equations, and figures of Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) alongside exact file and line numbers in upstream rust-v1-sim (planform.rs, params.rs, presets.rs). All 24 presets in PAPER_PRESETS map directly to numbered figures in Bressloff et al. (2001/2002), and Section 14 of morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean machine-checks the retino-cortical pullback classification, the 2*gamma_3(theta) > gamma_0 roll-stability criterion, and the +-1 Floquet multiplier return maps. However, the per-mode phase multipliers in planform_modes (0.35 for cobweb, -0.25 for rhombic, -1.0 and 0.5 for hex_pi) and preset sharpness values (1.8, 2.1, 2.3) are unmotivated upstream rendering heuristics with no citation or derivation from Bressloff et al. (-5 pts). Additionally, the README.md section for 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py misdescribes the code's contoured hexagonal FFT peak as moving to the sqrt(3)k ring (whereas the code and self-test show the dominant peak is at 2k) and omits the --sweep, --preset, and --hemifield-mode CLI flags (-4 pts). Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L313–L499: PAPER_PRESETS mapping all 24 preset IDs to Bressloff (2001/2002) figures <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L313-L499>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L615–L696: Traceability comments linking orientation_eigen_details and amplitude_gamma2/3 to Bressloff 2001 §4.2-§5 and upstream planform.rs:745-770 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L615-L696>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L982–L1014: planform_modes with undocumented per-mode phase multipliers (0.35, -0.25, -1.0, 0.5) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L982-L1014>; morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean L510–L596: Lean 4 Section 14 theorems for retino-cortical pullback, cubic roll stability, and Floquet period doubling <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean#L510-L596>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-code-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 9.1e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Model fidelity to source: 76/100" ;
    dct:references <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bressloff-v1-form-constants-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bressloff-v1-form-constants-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bressloff-v1-form-constants-3> ;
    rdfs:comment "The script accurately implements the intra-hypercolumn Fourier harmonics (Eq. 3.12), anisotropic Fourier- Bessel lateral coupling weights (Eq. 4.9), second-order Rayleigh-Schrödinger dispersion curves lambda_even/odd(q), and the exact two-regime log-polar retino-cortical map with analytic inverse and tangent orientation map phi_R = phi + theta_R, matching all 5 stability_reports and all 24 preset runs in paper- calibration.json to 2.22e-16. However, amplitude_gamma2 and amplitude_gamma3 compute only unweighted local orientation overlap integrals without the spatial lateral-kernel weighting, quadratic-mode feedback, or quintic terms of Bressloff et al. (2001 §5, Eqs. 5.12-5.15), which prevents rolls and squares from ever stabilizing, leaves odd-branch H0/Hpi degenerate (eta_hex = 0), and causes 12 of 133 paper-expectation checks to fail (-10 pts). In stability_scan and branch_selection_for, presets with fixed parity != critical_branch (such as fig29_* and fig30_*) evaluate the even eigenfunction at the odd branch's critical_q and growth rate, and roll_stable checks 2*gamma_3(theta) > gamma_0 only at the preset's rendering angle pattern_angle_deg rather than across all theta (falsely reporting roll_stable=True in CSV rows 9, 10, and 12) (-5 pts). Furthermore, _eval_xy maximizes |a(r, phi)| rather than signed activity a(r, phi), introducing sign-flip jumps across nodal lines that double the contoured hexagonal spatial frequency (k* = 21 vs 11 cycles), and orientation_eigen_details truncates at m=4 with an ad-hoc +-1.5 clamp vs m=10 in branch_coupling_sum (-5 pts). Finally, the wavenumber scaling k = q*/d_hyp with upstream alpha, beta, and xi_hat_lat = 1.5 yields a cortical wavelength lambda_c = 8.68 mm (11 cycles) that is 3.1x longer than the paper's 2.4-3.2 mm (30-36 stripes), and the Rule et al. (2011) panel has no dynamical or Floquet solver (-4 pts). Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L519–L599: Fourier harmonics W_n, Fourier-Bessel lateral coupling W_n^lat(q), and O(beta^2) perturbative dispersion relation branch_growth <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L519-L599>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L672–L859: Unweighted orientation-overlap integrals amplitude_gamma2/amplitude_gamma3 and branch_selection_for where roll_stable only tests pattern_angle_deg <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L672-L859>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L946–L960: stability_scan evaluates branch_selection_for at critical_q of critical_branch even when eff_params.parity is fixed to the opposite branch, and sets wave_number = critical_q / hypercolumn_mm <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L946-L960>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1069–L1093: _eval_xy selects argmax_phi |a(x, phi)| via np.abs(val) > np.abs(best), flipping signs across nodal boundaries <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1069-L1093>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Morphometric validation: 79/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The script computes 2D FFT spectral ring metrics (k*, ring sharpness, normalized azimuthal harmonics c2, c4-c2, c6-c2, and harmonic ring powers at k, sqrt(3)k, 2k), retinal pullback mirror-symmetry and seam- contrast diagnostics, a Gaussian-only negative control, an empirical cortical magnification comparison against Horton & Hoyt (1991) over 1-40 degrees (6.8% RMS relative error, 30.0% max relative error at 1 deg), and an anatomical scale check against Bressloff et al. (2002 §1.1). However, the main calibration checks benchmark against another software implementation's JSON output (paper-calibration.json) rather than digitized paper figures or empirical hallucination data, and on the paper's own anatomical/perceptual scale anchors the rendered planforms miss the 2.4-3.2 mm cortical wavelength and 30-36 stripe count by 3.1x (-10 pts). In retinal_pullback_diagnostics, seam_contrast divides |f[cy] - f[cy-1]| on the left meridian by the right meridian across v = 0, but for any y-even cortical planform at phase = 0 (both Cobweb and Honeycomb) f(+v) = f(-v) identically on both sides, producing NaN and mislabelling Cobweb and Honeycomb in the figure titles as 'seam n/a (y-independent)' despite strong y-dependence and a slope cusp on the left meridian (-6 pts). Finally, the Rule et al. (2011) Fig. 8 comparison merely reads upstream fixture curves that fail 4 of 6 acceptance checks (RMS beta error 0.154 vs 0.10 threshold, calibration_claim_allowed=false), and the FFT lattice classifier falls back to an undifferentiated 'mixed/rhombic' bucket for column V (-5 pts). Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L185–L256: compare_cortical_magnification against Horton & Hoyt (1991) and compare_paper_scale_anchors reporting the 3.1x wavelength discrepancy <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L185-L256>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1133–L1173: retinal_pullback_diagnostics computes row difference across v=0, yielding NaN for y-even Cobweb and Honeycomb planforms and attributing it to y-independence <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1133-L1173>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1178–L1259: spectral_ring_metrics and harmonic_ring_powers on the cortical grid with 'mixed/rhombic' fallback <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1178-L1259>; bressloff_v1_metrics.csv L1–L40: Exported metrics table recording 121/133 fixture checks passed, seam_contrast=nan on cobweb/honeycomb, and Rule 2011 outside-threshold-diagnostic <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/bressloff_v1_metrics.csv#L1-L40>. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): bressloff-v1-form-constants stability_reports parity, max |Δ| = 0.0 dimensionless (reference 0.0, MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants commit 344863a1bd9e8a8e8c9cb20aced2897f3ffb2c4c) [maximum absolute error across all 5 Bressloff (2001) stability_reports (q*, λ*, γ(0), γ(θ), η_hex) vs paper-calibration.json]; Mexican-hat lateral inhibition critical wavenumber q* (Bressloff 2001 Fig. 16) = 1.028 dimensionless wavenumber (reference >0.5 (finite Turing/Euclidean symmetry-breaking wavelength), Bressloff et al. 2001 Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 356:299 Fig. 16) [maximizer of max(λ_even(q), λ_odd(q)) with lateral_inhibition = 0.27] — interior peak prominence = 0.1200; Gaussian-only negative control critical wavenumber q* (lateral_inhibition = 0) = 0.05 dimensionless wavenumber (reference 0.05, q_min boundary of [0.05, 3.0] grid (monotonically decaying dispersion, prominence = 0.0)) [maximizer of λ(q) when Mexican-hat surround inhibition is removed (lateral_inhibition = 0.0)] — interior peak prominence = 0.00e+00; Klüver Tunnel/Rings cortical planform spectral ring sharpness = 31.331 ratio (peak/median PSD) (reference >5.0, Bressloff et al. 2001 Fig. 7 / Klüver 1966 Tunnel form constant) [2D FFT radial power spectrum peak/median ratio at k* = 11 cycles]; Klüver Honeycomb/Hex linear cortical planform spectral ring wavenumber k* = 11.0 cycles / domain (reference 11 (q*/d_hyp = 11.27 cycles), Bressloff et al. 2001 Fig. 35 / Klüver 1966 Honeycomb form constant) [dominant radial FFT wavenumber of the linear 3-mode hexagonal eigenmode superposition (non-contoured, weak tanh); the rendered wavenumber is q*/d_hyp quantised to integer cycles on the 2πβ/ε torus] — contoured-rendering k* = 21 = 2k harmonic of tanh∘max (normalised power at k/√3k/2k = 0.50/0.68/1.00); FFT lattice class = hexagonal; Retino-cortical magnification vs Horton & Hoyt (1991), RMS relative error over 1-40 deg = 0.0678 dimensionless (reference 0 (perfect agreement); map-implied A = α/ε = 18.72 mm/deg, E2 = w0/ε = 1.71 deg vs 17.3, 0.75, Horton & Hoyt 1991 Arch. Ophthalmol. 109:816 (doi:10.1001/archopht.1991.01080060080030); datasets/bressloff/horton_hoyt_1991_magnification.json) [RMS of (α/(w0+εr) − 17.3/(E+0.75)) / (17.3/(E+0.75)) over 157 eccentricities in [1, 40] deg] — max |rel err| = 0.300; fovea→90° extent 74.6 mm (model) vs 83.0 mm (H&H); Upstream fixture paper-expectation checks passed (paper-calibration.json, stability_reports + runs) = 121.0 count (reference 133.0, MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants commit 344863a1bd9e8a8e8c9cb20aced2897f3ffb2c4c, stability_reports[*].checks and runs[*].checks) [number of the fixture's own expected-vs-actual checks that pass, out of 133 (stability_reports 10/11, runs 111/122; run status {'pass': 17, 'review': 7})] — fig40_odd_hex_bifurcation/selected-pattern: expected triangle, actual honeycomb; fig31_square_even/same-lattice-branch-pattern: expected cobweb, actual spiral; fig31_square_even/same-lattice-branch-family: expected square, actual roll; fig32_square_odd/same-lattice-branch-pattern: expected cobweb, actual spiral; fig32_square_odd/same-lattice-branch-family: expected square, actual roll; fig35_hex_even/same-lattice-branch-pattern: expected hex_pi, actual honeycomb; fig36_triangle_odd/same-lattice-branch-pattern: expected triangle, actual honeycomb; fig5_hex_cortical/same-lattice-branch-pattern: expected hex_pi, actual honeycomb; fig5_square_cortical/same-lattice-branch-pattern: expected cobweb, actual spiral; fig5_square_cortical/same-lattice-branch-family: expected square, actual roll; fig6_visual_field_planforms/same-lattice-branch-pattern: expected cobweb, actual spiral; fig6_visual_field_planforms/same-lattice-branch-family: expected square, actual roll; Preset runs reproduced with exact parity (paper-calibration.json runs[]) = 24.0 count (reference 24.0, MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants commit 344863a1bd9e8a8e8c9cb20aced2897f3ffb2c4c, runs[*]) [runs whose critical_q, critical_branch, selected family/pattern/scope and rendered pattern match the fixture, out of 24] — max |Δq*| = 2.22e-16; Gallery panels whose rendered lattice is the branch the cubic amplitude equations select (rhombic angle free) = 1.0 count (reference 5.0, Bressloff et al. 2001 §5 cubic amplitude equations (Eqs. 5.9-5.15), evaluated by branch_selection_for()) [rendered family == unrestricted_selected_family, out of 5 gallery panels; 1 further panels are linearly stable branches that lose the Lyapunov tie-break, 3 are imposed (unstable at cubic order)] — fig7_lattice_tunnel: imposed-unstable; fig33_rhombic_even_roll: imposed-unstable; fig31_square_even: imposed-unstable; fig35_hex_zero_even: stable-coexisting; fig33_rhombic_even: selected; Rendered cortical wavelength λ_c relative to the paper's stated 2.4-3.2 mm = 3.1006 ratio (reference 1.0 (paper scale); paper also states 30-36 perceived stripes vs 11 rendered cycles, Bressloff et al. 2002 Neural Comput. 14:473 §1.1) [λ_c = 2π d_hyp / q* (d_hyp = 2 mm, q* from the gallery preset) divided by the midpoint 2.8 mm of Bressloff 2002 §1.1's 2.4-3.2 mm] — λ_c = 8.68 mm; foveal magnification 10.98 vs 11.5 mm/deg (α = 3/π from upstream params.rs vs α ≈ 1.00 implied by the paper); Spiral retinal pullback mirror symmetry (full-field convention) = -0.0291 Pearson r (reference 1.000 (bilateral-mirror mode, same preset), Bressloff et al. 2001 Fig. 33b / 2002 §1.1 (logarithmic spirals are oblique rolls under the complex-log map)) [correlation between the retinal field and its left-right reflection; chiral spirals give |r| << 1, the bilateral-mirror convention gives 1.0] — left-horizontal-meridian seam contrast 9.9x (full-field) vs 1.0x (mirror); Critical-branch parity flips over the lateral-spread sweep θ₀ ∈ [0°, 90°] = 2.0 count (reference ≥1 (Bressloff 2001 §4: even planforms selected for θ₀ ≳ 45°), Bressloff et al. 2001 Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 356:299 §4, Figs. 16-17) [number of even↔odd changes of the maximal-growth branch across 31 sweep points (fig17_even base)] — flips at θ₀ ≈ [45, 90]°; q* over ξ̂_lat 1.5→6: 1.46→0.70; Rule et al. (2011) Fig. 8 overlay domain-normalised RMS β error (diagnostic, no calibration claim) = 0.154 normalised wavenumber β (reference <= 0.10 acceptance threshold (NOT met), Rule, Stoffregen & Ermentrout 2011 PLoS Comput. Biol. 7:e1002158 Fig. 8 via upstream fixture) [rule-2011-floquet.json source_curve_comparison.domain_beta_mapping.rms_error] — acceptance_status = outside-threshold-diagnostic; calibration_claim_allowed = False." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-1>,
