<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — MorphoEval overall 80.9/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Blinded second-assessor pass. 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py is a transparent, machine-precision Python port of the upstream MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants Rust implementation covering perturbative Fourier- Bessel marginal stability, local-overlap cubic branch selection, the two-regime log-polar retino-cortical pullback with tangent orientation line elements, parameter sweeps, and an empirical magnification comparison against Horton & Hoyt (1991). While the script exemplifies honest scientific reporting by badging every gallery panel (SELECTED vs STABLE-coexisting vs IMPOSED-unstable), surfacing all 12 failed paper-expectation checks across the 5 stability reports and 24 preset runs, and quantifying its 3.1x cortical wavelength discrepancy against Bressloff et al. (2002), substantive modelling gaps remain. Specifically, the simplified local- orientation cubic integrals never stabilize rolls or squares anywhere in parameter space (requiring 3 of Klüver's 4 form constants to be manually imposed at identical coupling parameters), contoured planforms maximize |a(r, phi)| rather than signed activity a(r, phi), non-axis-aligned cortical modes are not quantized to integer azimuthal cycles on the y-periodic torus, and retinal_pullback_diagnostics returns NaN on y-even lattices (Cobweb and Honeycomb) while mislabelling them as y-independent. Overall 80.9/100 (faithfulness 75.9, reproducibility 92.5; model-implementation 76.0/100, biological-validation 75.9/100, applicable-only overall 80.9/100; uncalibrated rubric score, not a calibrated probability); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d6f3c94; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 76, Morphological realism / specimen match 74, Parameter expressivity 76, Morphometric validation 79, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 91, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: bressloff_v1_form_constants_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py at d6f3c94, image/png, 1634872 B, 2620×2419 px, artifact_sha256 799d93639f28fa0f81279848de4b8d23b26644a1c8856fdc44c0028d4fc6ba5e (sha256 799d93639f28fa0f81279848de4b8d23b26644a1c8856fdc44c0028d4fc6ba5e), spec_fingerprint fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7; artifact_sha256: 799d93639f28fa0f81279848de4b8d23b26644a1c8856fdc44c0028d4fc6ba5e; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/bressloff/driven-neural-fields-registry.json=4f07b5175a48bcb5..., datasets/bressloff/paper-calibration.json=af12b2c1aa3e38fa..., datasets/bressloff/rule-2011-floquet.json=5e349c7b80185de4...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Bressloff et al. (2001, 2002): a Euclidean shift-twist symmetric neural field on the orientation-hypercolumn lattice of V1 undergoes a Turing-type instability whose even (contoured) and odd (non-contoured) planforms, pulled back through the retino-cortical map x=(alpha/eps)ln(1+eps r/w0), y=beta r theta/(w0+eps r), give Klüver's four form constants; the 2002 paper states a foveal magnification of 11.5 mm/deg, 30-36 perceived stripes and a cortical wavelength of 2.4-3.2 mm | Ermentrout & Cowan (1979): cortical rolls map to tunnels, funnels and spirals under the log-polar retino-cortical map | Horton & Hoyt (1991): human V1 linear cortical magnification follows M(E) = 17.3/(E + 0.75) mm/deg | Rule, Stoffregen & Ermentrout (2011): periodic flicker drives 1:1 (stripe) and 2:1 period-doubling (hexagon) Floquet resonance tongues over forcing period and wave number | Tamekue, Prandi & Chitour (2024): a Gaussian-only (no Mexican-hat) lateral kernel produces no MacKay-type pattern, used here as the negative control; reconstructed_in_script: Fourier-Bessel lateral coupling, even/odd orientation eigenbranches and marginal-stability scans, cubic amplitude-equation coefficients gamma_0, gamma_3(theta), eta_hex with unrestricted branch selection (rhombic angle = argmin gamma_3) and per-panel SELECTED / STABLE-coexisting / IMPOSED-unstable badges, the exact two-regime retino-cortical map with analytic inverse in a full-field theta in (-pi, pi] convention (bilateral-mirror mode kept and compared, seam contrast and mirror symmetry quantified), an orientation field drawn as line elements in cortex and in the visual field via the tangent map phi_R = phi + theta_R, rendered wavenumber |k| = q*/d_hyp quantised to integer torus cycles, exact parity with all 5 stability_reports and all 24 preset runs of the upstream fixture with all 133 of its paper-expectation checks counted (121 pass), a comparison of the map's magnification with Horton & Hoyt (1991) and with the 2002 paper's own scale anchors, parameter sweeps over lateral width, lateral inhibition and lateral spread (CLI --sweep), a Gaussian-only negative control cross-referenced to the vendored registry, and a diagnostic overlay of the Rule (2011) tongue boundaries (16 curves over 5 forcing amplitudes) vendored from the upstream MesmerPrism fixture with its calibration status printed; transfer_boundary: Numerical parity to 2.2e-16 is with the MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants Rust implementation's stability_reports and runs, not with digitised figures of the 2001 paper; alpha = 3/pi and beta = 1.589/2 are the upstream params.rs values (foveal magnification 10.98 vs the paper's 11.5 mm/deg) and the rendered cortical wavelength 8.7 mm is 3.1x the paper's 2.4-3.2 mm — both are computed and printed, not corrected | Of the five gallery panels only the rhombic lattice is SELECTED by the cubic amplitude equations; the honeycomb is STABLE-coexisting and tunnel/spiral/cobweb are IMPOSED-unstable, because the bare orientation-overlap cubic coefficients make 2 gamma_3(theta*) < gamma_0 for every parameter value swept (rolls and squares never stable) | The full-field pullback carries a discontinuity on the left horizontal meridian (seam contrast 7-10x for oblique modes) because the theta in (-pi, pi] branch cut maps to a line in cortex; the bilateral-mirror alternative removes the seam but destroys spiral chirality (mirror symmetry 1.000); does_not_claim: Fifth-order resolution of the odd-branch hexagon/triangle degeneracy (Bressloff 2001 Section 5.2), the full cubic coefficients with firing-rate derivative weights and quadratic feedback (Eq. 5.15), a Floquet solver or validated reproduction of Rule (2011) Fig. 8 (the vendored fixture is marked diagnostic-only upstream and the script says so), derivation of contoured vs non-contoured from the critical local harmonic (contour_mode is a preset flag), or a comparison with subject drawings of hallucinations." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants> ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:1080-1092 — _eval_xy selects the contoured orientation via np.abs(val) > np.abs(best) (argmax_phi |a(x, phi)|) rather than signed activity argmax_phi a(x, phi), causing discontinuous sign flips across nodal lines that shift the contoured hexagonal FFT peak to the 2k harmonic (21 cycles vs 11 linear cycles).",
        "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:1156-1172 — retinal_pullback_diagnostics computes seam_contrast from |f[cy] - f[cy-1]| across v = 0, which vanishes identically on both meridians for any y-even planform at phase = 0 (Cobweb and Honeycomb), returning NaN and mislabelling both panels as 'seam n/a (y-independent)' at line 1957.",
        "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:672-695 — amplitude_gamma2 and amplitude_gamma3 compute only local orientation overlap integrals without the spatial lateral-kernel weighting, quadratic-mode feedback, or quintic terms of Bressloff et al. (2001 §5, Eqs. 5.12-5.15), so rolls and squares are never stable anywhere in parameter space and 3 of Klüver's 4 form constants in the gallery must be manually imposed.",
        "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:769-783 — in branch_selection_for, roll_stable tests 2*gamma_3(theta) > gamma_0 only at the preset's rendering angle pattern_angle_deg (clipped to [15, 75] deg) instead of across all theta (or theta_opt ~ 45 deg), falsely reporting roll_stable=True in bressloff_v1_metrics.csv lines 9, 10, and 12 whenever pattern_angle_deg is 0, 60, or 90 deg.",
        "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:931-959 — in stability_scan, when params.pattern != 'auto' and params.parity differs from critical_branch (e.g. fig29_* and fig30_* where parity='even' but critical_branch='odd'), branch_selection_for evaluates the even eigenfunction at the odd branch's critical_q and critical_growth.",
        "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:954-958 — setting wave_number_qstar = critical_q / hypercolumn_mm (with d_hyp = 2.0 mm and gallery q* = 1.4475) produces a cortical wavelength lambda_c = 8.68 mm (11 cycles on the 97.9 mm torus), 3.1x longer than Bressloff et al.'s (2002 §1.1) 2.4-3.2 mm (30-36 stripes), and only quantizes |k| rather than (k_x, k_y), leaving non-integer azimuthal cycles k_y*L/(2*pi) = 11*sin(theta) and a 9.9x left- meridian seam on oblique/spiral modes.",
        "remediation needed: README.md:431-442 — the ### [2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py] documentation is out of sync with the script: it claims 10/11 fixture checks pass (omitting the 122 runs[].checks with 11 failures), states that both hemispheres carry a bilateral-mirror mode by default (now full-field), attributes the contoured hex FFT shift to sqrt(3)k instead of 2k, and describes a 4x4 figure / 4-preset GIF / 17 self-test checks instead of the actual 4x5 figure / 5-preset GIF / 22 self-test checks and --sweep/--preset/--hemifield-mode flags." ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.09e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Parameter expressivity: 76/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The script provides parameter_sweep and a --sweep CLI flag covering six biophysical coupling parameters (lateral_wide_sigma, lateral_inhibition, lateral_spread_deg, lateral_sigma, eigen_beta, local_sigma_deg) and plots three sweeps in Panels F and G. Increasing lateral_wide_sigma from 1.5 to 6.0 monotonically lowers q* from 1.46 to 0.70, increasing lateral_inhibition from 0 to 1 monotonically raises q* from the 0.05 floor to 1.00, and sweeping lateral_spread_deg from 0 to 90 degrees induces two parity flips between odd and even branches at 45 and 90 degrees. However, all five gallery columns share the exact same biophysical coupling parameters (lateral_sigma=1.0, lateral_wide_sigma=1.5, lateral_inhibition=1.0, lateral_spread_deg=60.0, eigen_beta=0.35, giving identical q* = 1.447468 and 11 cycles) and differ solely via manual preset overrides of pattern and pattern_angle_deg (-12 pts). Moreover, across all six sweepable parameters, the unrestricted cubic branch selection remains locked to rhombic (roll_ever_stable=False and square_ever_stable=False everywhere), so sweeping the model's coupling parameters never drives transitions across Klüver's form- constant families (-8 pts). Finally, the lateral_spread_deg sweep in Panel G evaluates q* on a 128-point grid (step 0.0272) over which q* takes only three discrete values between 0.9465 and 1.0280, yielding a quantized step curve (-4 pts). Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L380–L460: Gallery presets in PAPER_PRESETS share identical coupling parameters and vary only pattern, pattern_angle_deg, and sharpness <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L380-L460>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1506–L1560: SWEEPABLE_PARAMS and parameter_sweep implementation over 6 coupling parameters <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1506-L1560>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1687–L1707: Sweep summaries confirming unrestricted_selected_family is solely rhombic and roll_ever_stable / square_ever_stable are always False <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1687-L1707>; bressloff_v1_metrics.csv L31–L43: CSV kluver_form_constant and parameter_sweep rows showing identical critical_q=1.447468 across all 5 gallery presets and 3-bin quantization in lateral_spread_deg <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/bressloff_v1_metrics.csv#L31-L43>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Reproducibility package: 93/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The script is completely deterministic (no stochastic state), verifies SHA-256 checksums for all four dataset files before executing, switches cleanly to the headless Agg backend when --no-show or --self-test is passed, and passes all 22 assertions in --self-test in ~18 seconds. Dependencies are specified in requirements.txt and locked with exact versions in requirements.lock.txt (Python 3.14.7, numpy==2.5.4, matplotlib==3.10.7, pillow==12.0.0, scipy==1.16.3). A 4-point deduction applies because README.md documents an outdated check count, runtime, and figure grid (17 checks in ~3 s, 4x4 grid, 4 GIF presets) while omitting --sweep, --preset, and --hemifield-mode, and requirements.lock.txt drops opencv-python and tifffile from requirements.txt due to a numpy>=2.3 dependency conflict (-4 pts). A further 3 points are deducted because passing --sweep PARAM --csv /path/out.csv writes to <stem>_sweep_<PARAM>.csv instead of the requested --csv path and silently exits before generating --csv or --out unless --out is also passed explicitly on the command line (-3 pts). Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L100–L116: Headless Agg backend selection and FIXTURE_CHECKSUMS SHA-256 dictionary <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L100-L116>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L2427–L2618: Deterministic self_test() suite executing 22 checks across fixtures, parity, pullback, FFT, sweeps, and anchors <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L2427-L2618>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L2621–L2680: CLI argument handling where --sweep rewrites the --csv filename and skips run_bressloff_analysis unless --out is explicitly supplied <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L2621-L2680>; requirements.lock.txt L1–L50: Pinned virtualenv lockfile noting omission of opencv-python and tifffile due to numpy==2.5.4 incompatibility <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/requirements.lock.txt#L1-L50>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-repro-package> ;
    pk:hasProbability 9.3e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Source and data traceability: 93/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "All seven primary literature sources (Bressloff et al. 2001, 2002; Ermentrout & Cowan 1979; Rule et al. 2011; Horton & Hoyt 1991; Tamekue et al. 2024; Klüver 1966) carry resolvable DOIs and PMIDs in the script header, datasets/bressloff/README.md, and datasets/bressloff/paper_citations.bib. All four JSON fixtures in datasets/bressloff/ are pinned by SHA-256 in FIXTURE_CHECKSUMS and attributed to commit 344863a1bd9e8a8e8c9cb20aced2897f3ffb2c4c of MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants under the MIT License, and RETINO_CONSTANT_PROVENANCE explicitly separates paper-derived constants (w0, eps from Drasdo 1977) from upstream Rust constants (alpha, beta). A deduction of 4 points applies because the numerical values RETINO_ALPHA = 3/pi and RETINO_BETA = 1.589/2 have no derivation beyond citing upstream params.rs, and driven-neural-fields-registry.json references two additional sources (nicks-et-al-2021 and bolelli- prandi-2025) that are omitted from paper_citations.bib (-4 pts). An additional 3 points are deducted because the top-level README.md section for this script has drifted out of sync with the code's provenance disclosures, still claiming '10/11 pass, and the one failure' (omitting the 122 runs[].checks with 11 failures) and stating that both hemispheres carry the same bilateral eigenmode by default (-3 pts). Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L11–L45: Primary sources with DOIs/PMIDs and upstream commit 344863a1bd9e8a8e8c9cb20aced2897f3ffb2c4c <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L11-L45>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L111–L152: FIXTURE_CHECKSUMS SHA-256 pins, RETINO_CONSTANT_PROVENANCE, and PAPER_SCALE_ANCHORS <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L111-L152>; datasets/bressloff/paper_citations.bib L1–L92: BibTeX entries for the 7 primary references, omitting Nicks et al. (2021) and Bolelli & Prandi (2025) from driven-neural-fields-registry.json <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/datasets/bressloff/paper_citations.bib#L1-L92>; README.md L428–L443: Outdated script walkthrough claiming 10/11 fixture checks, bilateral-mirror default, sqrt(3)k hex ring, and 4x4 / 4-preset layout <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/README.md#L428-L443>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-source-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 9.3e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Morphological realism / specimen match: 74/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The rendered gallery in bressloff_v1_form_constants_morphospace.png and docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif produces visually distinct cortical planforms and retinal pullbacks for Klüver's four form-constant families (Tunnel concentric rings, Spiral logarithmic arms, Cobweb radial/circular net, Honeycomb hexagonal lattice) plus the Rhombic lattice, complete with cortical and retinal orientation line segments. However, three of Klüver's four form constants (Tunnel, Spiral, Cobweb) are badged IMPOSED: unstable and Honeycomb is STABLE-coexisting because the model's cubic equations select only the 5th (Rhombic) column, so the classic form constants are produced by hard-coding mode wavevectors in planform_modes rather than emerging from the model (-10 pts). Because lambda_c = 8.68 mm is 3.1x longer than Bressloff et al.'s 2.4-3.2 mm scale (11 cycles vs 30-36 perceived stripes), the retinal pullbacks are roughly 3x coarser than Bressloff et al. (2001) Figs. 31-36 and (2002) Figs. 6-7 (-7 pts). In full-field mode, oblique and hexagonal cortical modes have non-integer azimuthal cycle counts k_y * L / (2*pi) = 11 * sin(theta) across the torus circumference L in addition to foveal narrowing, creating visible phase- discontinuity seams (9.9x on Spiral, 3.4x on Rhombic) and chevron kinks along the left horizontal meridian (-5 pts). Lastly, the contoured gallery panels plot continuous tanh heatmaps with sparse white line segments every 8 cells and the GIF drops contoured mode altogether (contour_mode='noncontoured'), departing from the paper's binary oriented-contour renderings (-4 pts). Evidence: bressloff_v1_form_constants_morphospace.png (generated output, not in repo): 5-column cortical and retinal gallery with orientation line segments, selection badges, and diagnostic panels A-G — bressloff_v1_form_constants_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py at d6f3c94, image/png, 1634872 B, 2620×2419 px, artifact_sha256 799d93639f28fa0f81279848de4b8d23b26644a1c8856fdc44c0028d4fc6ba5e (sha256 799d93639f28fa0f81279848de4b8d23b26644a1c8856fdc44c0028d4fc6ba5e), spec_fingerprint fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7; docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif (generated output, not in repo): 36-frame 5-preset phase-drift animation rendered in noncontoured mode with uniform_phase=True — docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif: rendered output of 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py at d6f3c94, image/gif, 2349709 B, 640×350 px, 36 frames, artifact_sha256 db057a32f49451a8c5ada9698336085308e9d3664d17769f51fa1cf4dda4dae8 (sha256 db057a32f49451a8c5ada9698336085308e9d3664d17769f51fa1cf4dda4dae8), spec_fingerprint fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L982–L1014: planform_modes hard-codes wavevector angles and amplitudes for rings, rays, spiral, cobweb, honeycomb, rhombic, hex_pi, and triangle <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L982-L1014>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1613–L1675: Gallery loop showing 1 selected, 1 stable-coexisting, and 3 imposed-unstable panels with 11 rendered cycles vs 30-36 paper stripes <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1613-L1675>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants (Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes)" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bressloff-v1-form-constants-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bressloff-v1-form-constants-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bressloff-v1-form-constants-3> ;
    schema:about "Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Fifth-order resolution of the odd-branch hexagon/triangle degeneracy (Bressloff 2001 Section 5.2), the full cubic coefficients with firing-rate derivative weights and quadratic feedback (Eq. 5.15), a Floquet solver or validated reproduction of Rule (2011) Fig. 8 (the vendored fixture is marked diagnostic-only upstream and the script says so), derivation of contoured vs non-contoured from the critical local harmonic (contour_mode is a preset flag), or a comparison with subject drawings of hallucinations",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Fourier-Bessel lateral coupling, even/odd orientation eigenbranches and marginal-stability scans, cubic amplitude-equation coefficients gamma_0, gamma_3(theta), eta_hex with unrestricted branch selection (rhombic angle = argmin gamma_3) and per-panel SELECTED / STABLE-coexisting / IMPOSED-unstable badges, the exact two-regime retino-cortical map with analytic inverse in a full-field theta in (-pi, pi] convention (bilateral-mirror mode kept and compared, seam contrast and mirror symmetry quantified), an orientation field drawn as line elements in cortex and in the visual field via the tangent map phi_R = phi + theta_R, rendered wavenumber |k| = q*/d_hyp quantised to integer torus cycles, exact parity with all 5 stability_reports and all 24 preset runs of the upstream fixture with all 133 of its paper-expectation checks counted (121 pass), a comparison of the map's magnification with Horton & Hoyt (1991) and with the 2002 paper's own scale anchors, parameter sweeps over lateral width, lateral inhibition and lateral spread (CLI --sweep), a Gaussian-only negative control cross-referenced to the vendored registry, and a diagnostic overlay of the Rule (2011) tongue boundaries (16 curves over 5 forcing amplitudes) vendored from the upstream MesmerPrism fixture with its calibration status printed",
        "reported_in_source: Bressloff et al. (2001, 2002): a Euclidean shift-twist symmetric neural field on the orientation-hypercolumn lattice of V1 undergoes a Turing-type instability whose even (contoured) and odd (non-contoured) planforms, pulled back through the retino-cortical map x=(alpha/eps)ln(1+eps r/w0), y=beta r theta/(w0+eps r), give Klüver's four form constants; the 2002 paper states a foveal magnification of 11.5 mm/deg, 30-36 perceived stripes and a cortical wavelength of 2.4-3.2 mm",
        "reported_in_source: Ermentrout & Cowan (1979): cortical rolls map to tunnels, funnels and spirals under the log-polar retino-cortical map",
        "reported_in_source: Horton & Hoyt (1991): human V1 linear cortical magnification follows M(E) = 17.3/(E + 0.75) mm/deg",
        "reported_in_source: Rule, Stoffregen & Ermentrout (2011): periodic flicker drives 1:1 (stripe) and 2:1 period-doubling (hexagon) Floquet resonance tongues over forcing period and wave number",
        "reported_in_source: Tamekue, Prandi & Chitour (2024): a Gaussian-only (no Mexican-hat) lateral kernel produces no MacKay-type pattern, used here as the negative control",
        "transfer_boundary: Numerical parity to 2.2e-16 is with the MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants Rust implementation's stability_reports and runs, not with digitised figures of the 2001 paper; alpha = 3/pi and beta = 1.589/2 are the upstream params.rs values (foveal magnification 10.98 vs the paper's 11.5 mm/deg) and the rendered cortical wavelength 8.7 mm is 3.1x the paper's 2.4-3.2 mm — both are computed and printed, not corrected",
        "transfer_boundary: Of the five gallery panels only the rhombic lattice is SELECTED by the cubic amplitude equations; the honeycomb is STABLE-coexisting and tunnel/spiral/cobweb are IMPOSED-unstable, because the bare orientation-overlap cubic coefficients make 2 gamma_3(theta*) < gamma_0 for every parameter value swept (rolls and squares never stable)",
        "transfer_boundary: The full-field pullback carries a discontinuity on the left horizontal meridian (seam contrast 7-10x for oblique modes) because the theta in (-pi, pi] branch cut maps to a line in cortex; the bilateral-mirror alternative removes the seam but destroys spiral chirality (mirror symmetry 1.000)" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1001/archopht.1991.01080060080030>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00336965>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.2000.0769>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1137/23M1616686>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1162/089976602317250861>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002158> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-10>,
